{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>הפעם הא'</b><br>כתמרות. [Like pillars] like תימורות, and perhaps it is so called because [they resemble] the heights of palm trees." "אבקת. Spices that are ground fine like dust." "רוכל. A merchant, like 'המה רוכליך' (they are your merchants)." "<b>הפעם הג'</b><br>מי זאת עולה מן המדבר. When she entered the Land, her fame went throughout the world, and this is the myrrh and frankincense, as though she is like מטתו שלשלמה (the litter of Solomon), in which every kind of spice is found."], :book :song-of-songs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {0 "Bracketed material [כמו עמודים] and [שהם דומות ל] appears in the source text as interlinear or marginal glosses; rendered as brackets to preserve their status."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra's commentary on the Canticles" "http://beta.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH002030344/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:44:10.352446717Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}